export const mainServiceSections = {
"sharai-nikah-without-registration": [["Nikah Without Civil Registration","Religious Validity And Civil Duties Are Different Questions","A couple may ask whether a religious Nikah requires a written government certificate as part of the religious contract. That is different from asking whether the applicable country requires marriage registration, a licence or prior civil formalities. Hanafi religious requirements must be assessed on their own terms, while Pakistan-connected marriages remain subject to the applicable registration framework. A religious-only service is assessed against the actual jurisdictions and proposed solemnisation arrangements."],["Religious-Only Nikah Service Scope","Discuss The Ceremony And Any Records Before Booking","Our team accepts religious-only enquiries from eligible overseas couples seeking to live according to their faith. The agreed service can involve the officiant, witnesses, consent review and any appropriate representation. Civil registration and government certificates are separate work unless expressly included. Identity verification and legally required records are not waived by calling the service undocumented. Confirm the fee, service scope and any records provided in writing before proceeding."],["Protection Of Spouses And Children","Explain The Religious Commitments And Civil Position","Nikah establishes religious commitments and the parties should understand the agreed Mahr and marriage conditions. Civil financial remedies, inheritance, immigration status and legal parentage depend on the applicable jurisdiction and evidence. A ceremony alone should not be advertised as guaranteeing every legal protection. Couples should review both spouses’ position and any children’s birth-registration requirements. Discuss children and family circumstances respectfully without using derogatory labels."]],
"islamic-nikah-witnesses": [["Hanafi Witness Numbers For Muslim Nikah","Two Men Or One Man And Two Women","For a Muslim Nikah under the Hanafi requirements described by the cited religious authorities, the witness composition is two eligible Muslim men or one eligible Muslim man and two eligible Muslim women. The latter is an alternative composition, not a general rule shared by every school of Islamic jurisprudence. One witness alone does not satisfy that stated requirement. Assess the full marriage arrangement rather than treating witness numbers as the only condition."],["Eligibility Of Islamic Nikah Witnesses","Adulthood, Sound Mind And Understanding","Witnesses must meet the applicable religious qualifications, including adulthood, Muslim faith and soundness of mind in the Hanafi Muslim-marriage context addressed here. Sound mind means capacity to understand what is happening, not a special intelligence or educational qualification. The witnesses must hear and understand the relevant offer and acceptance. The religious and statutory age requirements for the spouses are separate matters that also require review."],["Witnesses And Remote Nikah Arrangements","Confirm The Session And Attorney Or Proxy Structure","Do not assume that joining any video call automatically fulfils the religious witnessing requirements. The officiant should settle how the offer and acceptance will take place, who hears them, and whether an authorised representative will act in the relevant session. Where a spouse is absent, obtain advice on the appropriate proxy structure. Document review and agreed participation arrangements should be completed before sending ceremony invitations."]],
"sharai-nikah": [["Sharai Nikah As A Religious Marriage Contract","Consent And Offer And Acceptance","Sharai Nikah is a religious marriage contract that carries mutual responsibilities. Couples seeking to establish their relationship according to Islam should first confirm eligibility, voluntary consent, the intended spouse and the agreed Mahr. This page explains the Hanafi approach; requirements should not be presented as identical across all schools. Personal circumstances, existing marriages and any impediment require assessment before a ceremony is arranged."],["Oral Nikah And Written Records","A Written Certificate Is Different From The Religious Aqd","In the Hanafi framework, a properly concluded oral contract can satisfy the relevant religious requirements without making a government certificate the act that creates the religious aqd. This does not mean that every oral conversation establishes a Nikah or that recording the terms is unnecessary in practice. The required offer, acceptance, witnesses and eligibility must be addressed. Civil registration and official record duties remain separate legal questions."],["Sharai Nikah Service For Overseas Couples","Religious-Only Enquiries And Country Review","Right Law Associates accepts enquiries for religious-only Nikah assistance for eligible overseas couples. The proposed participation, witnesses and any attorney or proxy must be reviewed before booking. Confirm whether the engagement includes a ceremony, any private record or civil document work. No certificate package should be implied where it is not agreed. The applicable jurisdictions must be assessed because a religious ceremony does not automatically create civil marital rights."]],
"online-nikah-services-in-karachi-rawalpindi-islamabad-rahim-yar-khan-and-lahore": [["Online Nikah Documents Before Booking","Confirm Identity, Consent And Marital Status","Online Nikah begins with a review of both intended spouses’ identities, present locations, nationality, age and marital status. Send clear CNIC, NICOP or passport copies and disclose any previous marriage. Divorced or widowed applicants should provide the relevant dissolution or death record for assessment. Confirm the agreed Mahr and witness arrangements before setting a date. Where an existing marriage continues, obtain advice on the applicable permission requirements rather than treating a private consent letter as the complete process."],["Online Nikah Through An Attorney Or Proxy","Prepare Specific Authority Before The Ceremony","Where a spouse cannot attend the place of solemnisation, the legal team assesses the proposed attorney or proxy arrangement. The authority should identify the intended spouses, representative and permitted acts. Our team can prepare the appropriate affidavit or authority draft after reviewing the circumstances. Documents signed overseas may require execution, notarisation or consular formalities according to their intended use. A general commercial power of attorney should not be assumed to cover marriage. For a party in Pakistan, signing the relevant documents in person is recommended where practical."],["Online Nikah Ceremony And Witness Arrangements","A Video Call Is One Part Of The Process","The arranged ceremony must address free consent, offer and acceptance, the agreed Mahr and the applicable witness and representation requirements. A WhatsApp call, meeting invitation or screenshot alone is not the complete marriage record. Confirm who will participate, how identities will be checked and who will complete the Nikah Nama. Review spellings, identification numbers and marriage conditions before the document is finalised. Confidential handling is part of the service; clients should agree a secure method for sending personal records."],["Online Nikah Registration And Certificate Documents","Separate The Nikah Nama From The Computerised Certificate","Solemnisation, marriage registration and issuance of a computerised Marriage Registration Certificate are different stages. Section 5 of the Muslim Family Laws Ordinance, 1961 requires registration of Muslim marriages through the applicable registration framework. The legal team identifies the competent registrar and authority for the proposed arrangement. A scanned Nikah Nama does not establish that all registration steps or later certificate work are complete. Ask for the status of each stage and keep the official documents and acknowledgment records safely."],["Online Nikah Fees And Payment Terms","PKR 40,000–60,000 With A Written Service Scope","Our Online Nikah service fee is PKR 40,000–60,000 according to the agreed work and documentation requirements. Payment is 50% in advance and the remaining 50% after Nikah and registration. Obtain a written quotation that states the included ceremony arrangements, document preparation and registration assistance. Confirm whether courier, translation, attestation, official charges or later certificate services are included or separately payable. Mahr is an obligation agreed between the spouses and should be recorded separately from the professional service fee."],["Online Nikah Documents For Overseas Use","Check The Receiving Country Before Making Travel Plans","Couples in different countries should explain where the marriage documents will be used before booking. The receiving embassy, immigration authority or foreign civil registry may require certified translations, authentication, attestation or additional evidence. Pakistani registration does not automatically complete a foreign immigration application or guarantee recognition for every purpose. Official processing times are separate from the scheduled ceremony. Send the actual receiving authority’s checklist so the legal team can assess the document work and identify any steps outside the agreed service."],["Religious-Only Online Nikah For Overseas Couples","Faith-Based Solemnisation Without A Civil Certificate Package","Right Law Associates also accepts enquiries from overseas Muslim couples seeking a religious-only Online Nikah rather than a civil marriage-registration or certificate package. The purpose is to help eligible, freely consenting couples enter a Nikah in accordance with the applicable religious requirements, including the agreed Mahr and proper witness and participation arrangements. Availability is assessed against the countries involved, the place and method of solemnisation, and the applicable law. The service does not promise that a religious-only ceremony creates a legally recognised civil marriage."],["Religious-Only Online Nikah Service Scope","Confirm Witnesses, Consent And The Agreed Work","The religious-only service may include consultation, identity and eligibility review, coordination with the Nikah officiant, witnesses and any required attorney or proxy, and arrangement of the ceremony. A civil registration application, government marriage certificate, immigration documentation or attestation package is not included unless separately agreed and legally appropriate. Declining a certificate package does not dispense with identity checks or any legally required records. Obtain a separate written quotation; the registered-service payment milestone should not automatically be applied to a ceremony-only engagement."],["Religious Nikah And Civil Marriage Rights","Understand Religious Commitments And Statutory Protection","Couples may seek Nikah to live according to their faith and establish mutual religious and moral responsibilities. These commitments should be explained respectfully alongside the agreed Mahr and marriage conditions. Civil spousal rights concerning property, financial remedies, inheritance and immigration depend on the applicable law and legal status of the marriage. A religious-only ceremony does not itself guarantee those remedies or settle legal parentage and birth-registration requirements. Discuss the protection sought by each spouse before choosing the service; children should always be described with dignity."],["Where Registration Or Prior Civil Marriage Is Required","Check The Relevant Country Before Booking","Pakistan-connected solemnisation must be assessed against applicable marriage-registration requirements, including section 5 of the Muslim Family Laws Ordinance, 1961. For overseas couples, countries and US states have different rules concerning religious officiants, licensing, remote participation and civil recognition. England and Wales distinguish religious-only ceremonies from legally recognised marriages, and France imposes requirements concerning civil marriage before religious solemnisation. We therefore review the actual jurisdictions and arrangements rather than using overseas residence as a blanket exemption from registration or other legal duties."]],
"succession-certificate-in-pakistan-for-legal-heirs": [["Succession Certificate And Letter Of Administration","Separate Movable Assets From Immovable Property","An estate may contain bank balances, investments and real property. NADRA distinguishes succession certificates for movable assets from letters of administration for immovable property. List each asset and the institution holding its record before selecting the application. A certificate is a step in estate administration; the receiving bank or property authority may require further transfer documents."],["Documents For A Succession Application","Prepare The Identity And Estate Record","NADRA lists the death certificate, CNIC cancellation certificate, Family Registration Certificate and legal-heir details among its requirements. Gather identity records and an accurate asset schedule before filing. Compare names and dates across the records and disclose missing or inconsistent entries. Obtain the current application checklist for the relevant province rather than assuming that one set of documents covers every case."],["Legal Heirs And Application Authority","Include Every Person Entitled To Inherit","Identify all legal heirs before preparing authorizations or calculating proposed shares. Supply the complete family history and disclose earlier deaths, marriages and any pending inheritance dispute. An FRC helps with family identification but should be reviewed with the other estate records. Counsel should assess the applicable succession law and the application authority before documents are signed."],["Verification, Notice And Certificate Issuance","Plan The Application In Stages","The administrative process involves an application, heir and asset information, verification and public notice. Applicants should confirm the current verification arrangements and respond to any requests for additional material. An objection or incomplete record can change the route and timing. No fixed completion date should be promised before the application and relevant authority requirements have been reviewed."],["Overseas Heirs And Local Representation","Confirm Verification Before Preparing Authority","An overseas heir should provide identity details, location and available estate documents at the first consultation. NADRA's current guidance distinguishes in-person initiation from initiation through legal counsel in Sindh and Balochistan. Representation does not automatically dispense with heir verification. Confirm the available verification and attestation arrangements before preparing a power of attorney or making travel plans."],["Using The Certificate And Resolving Disputes","Check The Next Transfer Step","After issuance, compare the certificate with the heir names and asset details supplied in the application. Ask the bank, investment institution or property authority for its transfer requirements. Where entitlement, title or an application is disputed, obtain advice on the appropriate remedy and forum. Preserve the notice, certificate, original asset records and correspondence so that any further proceeding is based on a complete file."]],
"succession-certificate-letter-of-administration": [["Succession Certificate And Letter Of Administration","Separate Movable Assets From Immovable Property","An estate may contain bank balances, investments and real property. NADRA distinguishes succession certificates for movable assets from letters of administration for immovable property. List each asset and the institution holding its record before selecting the application. A certificate is a step in estate administration; the receiving bank or property authority may require further transfer documents."],["Documents For A Succession Application","Prepare The Identity And Estate Record","NADRA lists the death certificate, CNIC cancellation certificate, Family Registration Certificate and legal-heir details among its requirements. Gather identity records and an accurate asset schedule before filing. Compare names and dates across the records and disclose missing or inconsistent entries. Obtain the current application checklist for the relevant province rather than assuming that one set of documents covers every case."],["Legal Heirs And Application Authority","Include Every Person Entitled To Inherit","Identify all legal heirs before preparing authorizations or calculating proposed shares. Supply the complete family history and disclose earlier deaths, marriages and any pending inheritance dispute. An FRC helps with family identification but should be reviewed with the other estate records. Counsel should assess the applicable succession law and the application authority before documents are signed."],["Verification, Notice And Certificate Issuance","Plan The Application In Stages","The administrative process involves an application, heir and asset information, verification and public notice. Applicants should confirm the current verification arrangements and respond to any requests for additional material. An objection or incomplete record can change the route and timing. No fixed completion date should be promised before the application and relevant authority requirements have been reviewed."],["Overseas Heirs And Local Representation","Confirm Verification Before Preparing Authority","An overseas heir should provide identity details, location and available estate documents at the first consultation. NADRA's current guidance distinguishes in-person initiation from initiation through legal counsel in Sindh and Balochistan. Representation does not automatically dispense with heir verification. Confirm the available verification and attestation arrangements before preparing a power of attorney or making travel plans."],["Using The Certificate And Resolving Disputes","Check The Next Transfer Step","After issuance, compare the certificate with the heir names and asset details supplied in the application. Ask the bank, investment institution or property authority for its transfer requirements. Where entitlement, title or an application is disputed, obtain advice on the appropriate remedy and forum. Preserve the notice, certificate, original asset records and correspondence so that any further proceeding is based on a complete file."]],
  'divorce-law': [
    ['Divorce Law In Pakistan: Choose The Correct Legal Route','Separate Talaq, Khula And Dissolution Before Taking Action','Divorce law in Pakistan uses different legal routes depending on who seeks termination of the marriage, the facts relied upon and whether the matter is contested. Talaq initiated by a husband, khula sought through the Family Court and dissolution based on statutory grounds should not be treated as interchangeable procedures. Right Law Associates begins by reviewing the Nikah Nama, present marital status, residence of the parties, any earlier notices or proceedings and the relief actually required. This first classification matters because the forum, documents, notices and follow-up steps can differ materially.'],
    ['Talaq Notice And Union Council Procedure','Do Not Treat A Private Pronouncement As The Whole Legal Process','Where talaq is relied upon, the statutory notice and Union Council process should be examined carefully. Clients should provide the written notice, proof of dispatch or service, Nikah Nama details and any communication from the relevant Union Council or Arbitration Council. A verbal or private family communication should not be assumed to complete every legal requirement. The file should show what was communicated, when it was communicated and whether the prescribed administrative process was initiated. Later certificate work also depends on the underlying record being complete and consistent.'],
    ['Khula Through The Family Court','Prepare The Petition Around The Actual Marriage Record And Relief','Khula is a judicial route and requires a properly prepared Family Court case. The petition should accurately state the marriage particulars, parties, addresses, relevant history and the relief requested. Existing claims concerning maintenance, dower, dowry articles, custody or visitation should be identified before filing because they may require connected or separate treatment. The client should provide the Nikah Nama, identity documents, any earlier notices and a concise chronology. Advice on financial consequences should be based on the terms of the marriage contract and facts rather than a generic assumption.'],
    ['Dissolution On Legal Grounds','Match The Claimed Ground With Evidence And Procedure','A spouse may seek dissolution on a recognised legal ground where the facts support that route. The legal team should identify the ground relied upon, the evidence available and whether another pending case affects the strategy. Medical records, maintenance history, correspondence, criminal or civil proceedings and prior court orders may become relevant depending on the allegation. A pleading should not include dramatic or unsupported accusations merely for emphasis; each material fact should be capable of being explained and, where necessary, proved through admissible evidence.'],
    ['Dower, Maintenance And Post-Divorce Financial Issues','Review Financial Rights Separately From Marital Status','Ending the marriage does not automatically resolve every financial issue between the spouses. Unpaid dower, maintenance, dowry articles, gifts, property claims and expenses for children may require separate assessment. The Nikah Nama should be read carefully for the agreed Mahr and any special conditions. Payment records, receipts, bank transfers, lists of articles and earlier settlements should be preserved. The appropriate remedy can depend on whether the claim arises from the marriage contract, a Family Court entitlement, ownership evidence or another legal basis.'],
    ['Divorce Registration And Certified Records','Complete The Record After The Legal Step Is Finished','After the legal termination route has been completed, clients often need documentary follow-up for remarriage, immigration, banking, inheritance or foreign use. The decree, Union Council record, certificate and identity particulars should be checked for consistency before they are submitted elsewhere. A computerized or certified record should not be requested on assumptions about the earlier file. If names, dates or marital particulars are inconsistent, identify the correction route before the document is used for another legal purpose. Preserve complete copies of notices, orders, acknowledgments and certificates.'],
  ],
  'divorce-lawyer-for-khula-divorce': [
    ['Divorce And Khula Lawyers: Start With A Case Assessment','Identify The Objective, Forum And Immediate Risk','A divorce or khula case should begin with a focused assessment rather than a standard petition. The lawyer needs the marriage record, present residence of both parties, any children, financial claims, previous notices, existing court cases and the client’s immediate objective. Urgent issues such as safety, access to children, maintenance or threatened disposal of property should be identified at the first consultation. Right Law Associates uses this initial review to separate the marriage-termination issue from connected claims and to prepare the correct litigation or documentation plan.'],
    ['Khula Petition Drafting And Family Court Representation','Build The Pleading Around Accurate Facts And Documents','A khula petition should state the marriage particulars and relevant facts clearly, without unnecessary allegations that do not assist the court. Accurate addresses are important for service and delay can result where parties or records are wrongly identified. The legal team should review the Nikah Nama, CNIC records, any prior correspondence and connected family proceedings before filing. During the case, clients should keep copies of summons, orders and hearing dates and inform counsel promptly about any new development affecting settlement, children or financial claims.'],
    ['Divorce Documentation For Husband-Initiated Talaq','Coordinate Notice, Administrative Record And Certificate Work','Where a husband initiates talaq, legal assistance may involve reviewing the written notice, the competent Union Council or local authority, service evidence and the later documentary record. The legal team should ensure that names, addresses and marriage particulars are consistent with the Nikah Nama and identity records. Clients should retain proof of submission and all authority correspondence. A later divorce certificate should reflect a properly completed underlying process; certificate work should not be used to conceal or bypass a missing legal step.'],
    ['Connected Family Claims During Divorce Or Khula','Plan Maintenance, Dower, Dowry And Child Issues Early','Marriage termination may occur alongside maintenance, dower, dowry-article, custody, guardianship or visitation disputes. These issues should be mapped at the outset so that documents and evidence are not lost while attention is focused only on the divorce decree. Financial claims may require proof of agreed Mahr, payments, household expenses, income or ownership of articles. Child-related claims require a separate welfare-focused assessment. A coordinated litigation plan can reduce contradictory pleadings and help the client understand which issues can be resolved together and which need distinct proceedings.'],
    ['Evidence, Hearings And Settlement Strategy','Preserve The Record And Document Any Compromise Carefully','Family cases often turn on the quality of the record as much as the allegations made. Preserve original documents, reliable copies, messages, payment evidence and earlier orders. If settlement discussions occur, the proposed terms should clearly state what is resolved and what remains pending. Agreements concerning dower, maintenance, custody, visitation or property should not be left to vague oral understandings where enforceability may later matter. Counsel should also explain the effect of withdrawing, compromising or not pursuing a pending claim before the client signs a statement.'],
    ['After The Decree Or Completion Of Talaq','Finish Registration, Enforcement And Future Documentation','Obtaining a decree or completing the talaq process may be only one stage. The client may still need certified copies, Union Council records, a divorce certificate, enforcement of financial relief or follow-up concerning children. Overseas clients may require attestation, translation or additional verification according to the receiving authority. The legal team should compare all final documents for consistent names and dates and advise which originals should be retained. A complete closing file reduces difficulty if remarriage, immigration, inheritance or later litigation requires proof of marital status.'],
  ],
  'child-custody': [
    ['Child Custody In Pakistan: Welfare Comes First','Assess The Child’s Circumstances Rather Than Relying On One Factor','Child custody disputes should be approached around the welfare and best interests of the minor. Age, gender and parental relationship may be relevant, but no single factor should be treated as automatically decisive without considering the child’s actual circumstances. The legal team should review the present care arrangement, schooling, health, emotional needs, safety concerns, parental involvement and any earlier orders. A parent seeking custody or resisting a change should provide a clear chronology and avoid turning the child into evidence in the dispute.'],
    ['Custody Applications And Court Preparation','Present A Practical Care Plan Supported By Records','A custody case should explain not only why the present arrangement is disputed but also what practical arrangement is proposed. School records, medical information, residence details, communication history and evidence of day-to-day care can help the court understand the child’s position. The applicant should disclose earlier guardianship or family proceedings and provide complete copies of relevant orders. Allegations about the other parent should be specific and supported where possible. A workable care plan is generally more useful than broad statements that one parent is simply better.'],
    ['Guardianship Proceedings And Legal Authority','Distinguish Physical Custody From Formal Guardianship','Physical custody and legal guardianship can overlap, but they are not always the same issue. A parent or relative may need formal authority for education, travel, documents, property or another legal purpose even where the child already lives with them. The lawyer should identify the precise order required and the court or authority concerned. Identity records, birth documents, family relationship evidence and existing custody arrangements should be reviewed before filing. Where a child owns property, additional safeguards and court supervision may become relevant.'],
    ['Visitation And Contact Arrangements','Create A Child-Focused Schedule That Can Be Followed','Where one parent has primary physical care, the other parent may seek structured visitation or contact. A useful proposal should address frequency, timing, location, holidays, school commitments, travel and communication in a way that is realistic for the child. Repeated last-minute disputes can be reduced when an order or settlement is clear. Parents should preserve relevant communication but should not use the child as a messenger between adults. If safety concerns exist, counsel should raise them through the proper legal process instead of unilaterally creating uncertainty.'],
    ['Evidence In Child Custody Cases','Focus On Welfare Evidence Rather Than Personal Attacks','Custody litigation should remain centred on the minor. Useful evidence may include school attendance, medical records, living arrangements, caregiving history, financial support, communication concerning the child and compliance with earlier orders. Personal disputes between the parents matter only to the extent they affect welfare, safety or the ability to care for the child. The legal team should separate provable events from suspicion or anger. Where expert, medical or other specialised material is relevant, the way it is obtained and presented should be considered before relying on it.'],
    ['Enforcement, Modification And Overseas Issues','Review New Circumstances And Existing Orders Before Acting','A custody or visitation order may later require enforcement or variation when circumstances materially change. Relocation, school changes, health concerns, repeated denial of contact or new safety issues should be documented promptly. A parent should obtain advice before removing a child from the jurisdiction or assuming an existing order no longer applies. Overseas families may also face immigration, travel-consent and foreign-order questions. The correct strategy depends on the wording of the current order, the child’s location and the court that retains jurisdiction over the matter.'],
  ],
  'legal-guardianship-laws-of-pakistan': [
    ['Legal Guardianship In Pakistan','Identify Why Formal Guardianship Is Required','A guardianship application should begin with the legal purpose for which authority is required. The issue may concern the person of a minor, education, medical decisions, travel, documentation, property or another matter requiring formal recognition. Existing parental rights and custody arrangements should be reviewed before assuming that a new guardianship order is necessary. Right Law Associates examines the child’s family position, current care, identity documents and any earlier proceedings so the application seeks an order that corresponds to the actual legal need.'],
    ['Appointment Of A Guardian','Provide A Complete Family And Care Record','The court’s consideration of guardianship should be supported by an accurate picture of the minor’s family, present residence and welfare. Applicants should disclose living parents, existing guardians, close relatives and any competing claim. Birth records, identity documents, death certificates where relevant and evidence of current care should be organised before filing. A person seeking appointment should be prepared to explain their relationship with the child, practical ability to act and the reason formal authority is required rather than relying only on family agreement.'],
    ['Natural Guardians And Custody Arrangements','Do Not Treat Family Status And Court Authority As Identical','Family relationships can create important rights and responsibilities, but a particular administrative or legal transaction may still require a formal order or documented authority. A child may reside with one relative while another person retains a recognised legal role. The legal team should identify whether the issue is custody, guardianship, consent, representation or property management. This distinction affects the documents and relief required. Existing court orders, parental consents and official records should be reviewed together before preparing a new application.'],
    ['Guardianship Of A Minor’s Property','Protect The Child’s Assets And Follow Court Requirements','Where a minor owns or is entitled to property, money, inheritance or another valuable asset, the proposed guardian’s authority should be defined carefully. Transactions involving a minor’s property may require court supervision or specific permission, and an adult should not assume that family control permits unrestricted sale, transfer or use. The asset record, title documents, inheritance papers and proposed transaction should be disclosed at the outset. Advice should focus on preserving the minor’s interest and documenting every step that requires judicial or administrative approval.'],
    ['Court Supervision, Reporting And Restrictions','Understand That Guardianship Carries Continuing Duties','Appointment as guardian can create responsibilities that continue after the initial order. Depending on the nature of the authority, the guardian may need to preserve records, account for property, obtain permission for significant decisions or comply with later directions. The exact duties depend on the order and applicable law. Clients should keep certified copies of the guardianship order and any subsequent permissions. Where circumstances change, the existing order should be reviewed rather than assuming the guardian can expand the scope of authority without further approval.'],
    ['Termination, Change Or Dispute Over Guardianship','Return To The Existing Order And Current Welfare Position','Guardianship may later be challenged, modified or brought to an end because of changed circumstances, the child reaching the relevant age, restoration of parental care or concerns about the guardian’s conduct. Any application should identify the current order, the change relied upon and the effect on the minor. The court may need updated welfare, residence or property information. Parties should avoid informal arrangements that contradict an existing judicial order. A complete procedural record helps counsel assess whether enforcement, variation, replacement or termination is the appropriate next step.'],
  ],
  'maintenance-in-pakistan': [
    ['Maintenance Law In Pakistan','Identify The Person Claiming Support And The Period In Issue','Maintenance claims can concern a wife, child or another person with a legally recognised entitlement, and the evidence required depends on the relationship and period claimed. Right Law Associates begins by reviewing the marriage or family record, ages of children, present living arrangements, earlier payments and any existing court orders. The client should state whether the claim is for current support, arrears, interim relief or enforcement. Separating these questions at the outset helps avoid a pleading that mixes different periods and legal bases without clear supporting evidence.'],
    ['Child Maintenance Claims','Document The Child’s Reasonable Needs And Existing Support','A child-maintenance case should present the child’s actual needs in a clear and organised way. School fees, medical expenses, food, housing, transport and other recurring costs may be relevant depending on the circumstances. Payment records should also be disclosed so the court can see what support has already been provided. The amount claimed should be connected to evidence rather than selected as an unexplained figure. Where custody or visitation is also disputed, those proceedings should be coordinated without using maintenance as leverage over the child’s relationship with either parent.'],
    ['Wife Maintenance And Marital Status','Review The Marriage, Separation And Relevant Conduct Carefully','A wife-maintenance claim requires review of the marriage record, living arrangements, date and circumstances of separation, prior payments and any pending divorce or khula proceedings. Legal consequences can depend on facts that should not be reduced to slogans about entitlement or fault. The Nikah Nama, notices, correspondence and previous orders may be important. Where dower or dowry claims also exist, those rights should be identified separately so that one financial issue is not mistakenly treated as resolving every other claim arising from the marriage.'],
    ['Interim Maintenance During Family Proceedings','Prepare Evidence For Immediate Support Requests','Family litigation can continue while day-to-day expenses still arise. Where interim maintenance is legally available, the application should present the immediate need and relevant financial material at an early stage. Clients should bring evidence of recurring expenses and any available information concerning the paying party’s income or resources. The opposing party should likewise provide a documented response rather than simply denying capacity. Interim directions should be read carefully because non-compliance can affect later proceedings and may require enforcement action.'],
    ['Income, Expenses And Financial Evidence','Use Reliable Records And Explain Gaps Honestly','Maintenance cases often involve disagreement about earnings and household expenditure. Salary slips, bank statements, business records, tax documents, school invoices, rent records and medical bills can assist where relevant. Not every person has a simple salaried income, so the evidence should reflect the actual financial position rather than a fictional monthly figure. If information is incomplete, counsel should explain what is known and what must be obtained through the legal process. Clients should avoid altering or selectively presenting records because credibility can affect the entire case.'],
    ['Execution And Recovery Of Maintenance Orders','Treat A Court Order As The Start Of Compliance Work, Not The End','After maintenance is ordered, payment history should be recorded carefully. Keep receipts, bank transfers, court deposits and copies of orders so arrears can be calculated accurately. Where an order is not followed, the available enforcement route depends on the court and procedural stage. A party seeking recovery should provide the complete order and a clear schedule of payments received and missed. A party claiming compliance should preserve equivalent proof. If circumstances later change materially, obtain advice on the appropriate application rather than simply stopping or varying payment unilaterally.'],
  ],
  'civil-law': [
    ['Civil Lawyers For Claims, Defence And Court Proceedings', 'Begin With The Relief Your Civil Case Requires', 'Civil litigation should begin by identifying the right being asserted and the order needed to protect it. A dispute concerning unpaid money, a challenged document, interference with possession or a contractual obligation may require different pleadings and evidence. Right Law Associates reviews the chronology, parties and available records before recommending a suit or response. Clients should disclose existing proceedings, settlements and earlier orders so that the proposed case does not conflict with the record.'],
    ['Civil Suits For Declaration And Cancellation', 'Identify The Document Or Right Being Challenged', 'A person contesting an ownership claim or a disputed instrument should provide the complete document and explain how it affects their rights. Counsel must consider whether declaration alone is appropriate or whether cancellation, possession or other consequential relief should also be sought. The assessment includes necessary parties, jurisdiction, limitation and the evidence supporting the challenge. A disagreement with a document’s contents is different from an allegation that it was forged or executed without authority.'],
    ['Civil Lawyers For Recovery And Contract Disputes', 'Organise The Agreement, Payments And Communications', 'For a recovery claim, preserve contracts, invoices, bank records, acknowledgments and correspondence that show the obligation and outstanding balance. Identify the party that actually entered the agreement rather than assuming that every director, employee or intermediary is personally liable. Counsel should examine dispute-resolution clauses, previous demands and the relevant time limits. Where the opposing party disputes delivery, performance or settlement, those issues should be addressed in the evidence and pleadings from the outset.'],
    ['Civil Injunctions And Interim Protection', 'Explain The Immediate Threat To The Court', 'An application for interim protection should identify the threatened conduct and the documents supporting the right asserted. The court’s assessment depends on the applicable legal requirements and the circumstances proved before it. An injunction should be coordinated with the main claim, including the parties and final relief requested. Clients should provide earlier orders and describe any urgent event accurately. Once an order is made, its wording and duration should be understood before taking a further step.'],
    ['Civil Court Evidence, Hearings And Case Management', 'Preserve Originals And Record Important Dates', 'Civil proceedings can involve service, written responses, issues, evidence, arguments and subsequent enforcement. Preserve original documents and identify witnesses who personally know the relevant facts. A clear chronology helps counsel distinguish documents created at the time from later explanations. Keep the legal team informed of notices and hearing dates rather than waiting until a deadline is close. The correct procedural response depends on the current stage and the exact order made by the court.'],
    ['Civil Decrees, Execution And Appeal Advice', 'Plan What Happens After The Judgment', 'A favourable judgment may require execution before the ordered payment or other relief is obtained. Obtain the relevant decree, certified copies and subsequent orders so that counsel can assess the appropriate application. A party considering an appeal should seek prompt advice because the forum, available grounds and time limits depend on the order concerned. An appeal does not automatically suspend enforcement. Any request for a stay requires a separate assessment of the legal route and supporting material.'],
  ],
  'corporate-tax-law-services': [
    ['Corporate Lawyers And Tax Lawyers For Business Decisions', 'Coordinate Legal Documents With Financial Records', 'A business decision may affect contracts, ownership, corporate filings and taxation at the same time. Right Law Associates starts by identifying the entity, transaction and compliance issue before recommending incorporation, restructuring or a filing response. Accounts and supporting records should be consistent with the legal documents and the actual activity. Clients should disclose pending notices, previous filings and agreed commercial terms so that the proposed approach addresses the whole business position rather than one isolated form.'],
    ['Corporate Law Advice On Business Structure', 'Compare Ownership, Management And Compliance Needs', 'Choosing a structure requires examination of the proposed owners, liability arrangements, funding and operational requirements. A company, partnership or another lawful form may involve different documents and continuing obligations. The name, proposed activities and regulatory permissions should be checked before applications are prepared. Counsel should also address who can sign, how decisions will be made and what happens if an owner leaves. A registration certificate does not replace the commercial agreement needed between the participants.'],
    ['Corporate Lawyers For SECP Incorporation', 'Prepare The Name And Incorporation Application', 'SECP’s company-registration guidance describes name reservation and incorporation applications through eZfile or the applicable physical process. The proposed entity and its documents must comply with the Companies Act, 2017 and relevant regulations. Identity, ownership, registered-office and constitutional-document requirements should be checked for the selected company type. Regulatory approval or licensing may also be necessary for particular activities. Our related company-registration page addresses the incorporation service, while this page covers the broader coordination of corporate and tax matters.'],
    ['Tax Lawyers For Registration And Return Review', 'Check The Taxpayer Record And Supporting Documents', 'Tax compliance begins with the taxpayer’s identity, registration position and actual sources of income or business activity. FBR registration and income-tax filing use Iris, subject to the applicable requirements. Before filing, reconcile the relevant accounts, withholding records and supporting information rather than relying on estimates. Where a wealth statement is required, it should be assessed alongside the return. Keep submission evidence and check the completed filing status; entering information into a draft should not be treated as completion.'],
    ['Tax Lawyers For Notices And Disputed Orders', 'Review The Notice, Deadline And Earlier Record', 'Send a complete copy of the notice or order, the date of receipt, earlier filings and any previous correspondence. The response must address the actual questions and documents requested. Available remedies and deadlines depend on the law and procedural stage, so a generic reply or an unrelated appeal form may be unsuitable. Counsel can coordinate factual explanations with accounting material and identify missing evidence. Preserve acknowledgment of submissions and subsequent communications so that the file records what was provided and when.'],
    ['Corporate Contracts, Shareholder Arrangements And Records', 'Document Authority And Commercial Obligations', 'Business agreements should identify the parties, scope, consideration, performance duties, termination terms and method of resolving disputes. Shareholder or management arrangements may also need decisions concerning authority, capital, transfer restrictions and access to records. The terms should be consistent with the entity’s constitutional documents and statutory obligations. Before signing, explain the intended commercial outcome and disclose side agreements or existing commitments. This allows counsel to identify conflicting obligations and prepare documents that can be implemented in practice.'],
  ],
  'fbr-income-tax-return-filing-lawyers-pakistan': [
    ['Income Tax Return Filing Lawyers In Pakistan', 'Start With The Taxpayer Record And Actual Sources Of Income', 'Income tax return filing should begin with the taxpayer’s CNIC or registration profile, sources of income, withholding information and supporting records for the relevant tax year. Right Law Associates reviews the legal and documentary position before submission so the return reflects the client’s actual circumstances. Salary, business income, property income, capital gains and other taxable or reportable items may require different treatment. A return should not be prepared by copying a previous year where the facts have changed.'],
    ['FBR Iris Registration, NTN And Profile Review', 'Confirm Registration Details Before Filing The Return', 'FBR filing is carried out through the applicable electronic system and depends on a correct taxpayer profile. Names, CNIC or registration details, addresses, business information and contact data should be checked before filing. An NTN, registration number or account login does not by itself establish that all compliance is complete. Where the profile contains an error or an old business status, the correction route should be identified before it causes inconsistencies in the return or later correspondence.'],
    ['Income Records, Withholding Taxes And Supporting Evidence', 'Reconcile Certificates, Bank Records And Business Accounts', 'Before filing, gather salary certificates, withholding evidence, bank information, business accounts, rent records, investment statements and other documents relevant to the taxpayer. Amounts should be reconciled rather than estimated merely to complete a form. Tax deducted or collected at source should be checked against available evidence and the electronic record. Where accounts or transaction documents do not match the proposed return, the discrepancy should be reviewed before submission.'],
    ['Wealth Statement And Asset Reconciliation', 'Explain Assets, Liabilities And Year-To-Year Movement', 'Where a wealth statement is required, assets, liabilities, personal expenditure and changes from the previous year should be reviewed together. Property, vehicles, bank balances, investments, loans and other material items may affect reconciliation. A figure entered in one schedule can have consequences elsewhere in the filing record. Clients should disclose major purchases, sales, gifts, inheritances and transfers so the legal and tax team can assess the supporting documentation and consistency of the statement.'],
    ['ATL And Filer Status After Income Tax Return Filing', 'Treat Submission And Active Taxpayer Status As Separate Checks', 'Submitting a return and appearing on the Active Taxpayers List are related but distinct matters governed by the applicable FBR rules and timing. Keep the electronic acknowledgment and confirm the completed filing status after submission. Where surcharge, late filing or another compliance issue affects ATL status, the applicable requirement should be checked rather than promising immediate filer status. The client should also preserve the final return and wealth statement for future notices, banking and transaction records.'],
    ['FBR Notices, Amendments And Tax Disputes', 'Respond To The Actual Notice And Procedural Deadline', 'If FBR issues a notice, order or information request, send the complete document and the date of service before preparing a response. The correct remedy depends on the statutory provision, stage and earlier filing history. A generic reply can miss the issue raised by the authority. Right Law Associates can coordinate legal submissions with accounting records, identify missing evidence and advise on amendment, reply, appeal or other available procedure where the facts and law support it.'],
  ],
  'company-registration-service-karachi': [
    ['Company Registration Services In Karachi', 'Choose The Business Structure Before Filing With SECP', 'Company registration should start with the proposed owners, business activity, capital plan, management structure and expected compliance needs. A private limited company, single member company or another lawful structure can create different governance and documentation requirements. Right Law Associates reviews the intended business before incorporation so the selected structure fits the commercial objective rather than merely producing a registration certificate.'],
    ['SECP Company Name Reservation And Incorporation', 'Check The Proposed Name, Activity And Regulatory Position', 'The incorporation process includes selecting an acceptable company name and submitting the required information and documents through the applicable SECP system. A proposed name should be checked for availability and regulatory restrictions. Businesses in regulated sectors may require additional approvals or licensing. The incorporation application should identify the company type, subscribers, directors, registered office and principal business activity accurately so later corporate and tax records remain consistent.'],
    ['Memorandum, Articles And Ownership Documents', 'Document The Company’s Objects, Authority And Internal Rules', 'The constitutional and ownership record should reflect the actual business arrangement. Memorandum and articles, subscriber information, director details and beneficial ownership information should be prepared or reviewed for the selected company type and current legal requirements. Where founders have separate commercial understandings concerning investment, management, profit distribution or exit, those arrangements may require additional agreements instead of relying only on standard incorporation documents.'],
    ['Registered Office, Directors And Beneficial Ownership', 'Keep Corporate Records Consistent After Incorporation', 'A company must maintain accurate information concerning its registered office, directors, members and other reportable corporate particulars. Changes should be documented and filed through the legally applicable procedure. The registered office should be a genuine address for corporate communication, and persons accepting office should understand their responsibilities. Beneficial ownership and control information should be assessed against current statutory and regulatory requirements rather than treated as a one-time incorporation formality.'],
    ['FBR Registration And Post-Incorporation Tax Setup', 'Coordinate SECP Records With Tax And Banking Requirements', 'After incorporation, the company may require tax registration, profile completion, bank documentation and other operational registrations according to its activity. Names, addresses, directors and business descriptions should remain consistent between corporate, tax and banking records. Right Law Associates coordinates the legal side of incorporation with tax advisers where required so post-registration steps are not left disconnected from the company’s actual operations and transaction records.'],
    ['Annual Compliance And Corporate Changes', 'Plan Returns, Share Changes And Governance Before Deadlines', 'Incorporation creates continuing obligations. Companies may need annual filings, accounts, resolutions and updates when directors, shareholders, registered office, capital or other particulars change. A proposed share transfer, new investor, restructuring or change of business should be reviewed before documents are signed. Keeping statutory records and approvals in order can reduce later disputes and make banking, investment, tax and due-diligence work easier to manage.'],
  ],
  'property-disputes': [
    ['Property Dispute Lawyers For Title And Ownership Claims', 'Start With The Chain Of Title And The Relief Required', 'A property dispute should begin with the documents said to create or transfer ownership and the exact order the client needs. Registered instruments, allotment or lease records, mutation entries, powers of attorney, inheritance documents and prior court orders may point in different directions. Right Law Associates reviews the complete chain rather than relying on possession or one recent document alone. The legal strategy may involve declaration, cancellation, possession, injunction, partition or another remedy depending on the record and parties involved.'],
    ['Possession Disputes And Illegal Occupation', 'Identify The Occupier’s Legal Status Before Filing', 'A person in possession may be an owner, co-owner, tenant, licensee, family member or alleged trespasser. Those positions can require different remedies and forums. Preserve photographs, notices, tenancy documents, utility records, correspondence and evidence showing when possession changed. Clients should avoid force or self-help eviction that may create further legal exposure. Where urgent interference or dispossession is threatened, counsel should assess whether interim protection is available and which main proceeding should accompany it.'],
    ['Partition And Co-Ownership Property Disputes', 'Establish Shares, Possession And Whether Physical Division Is Practical', 'Co-owners may disagree about use, rent, sale, construction or division of jointly held property. The first step is to identify every co-owner and the basis of each share. Urban buildings, inherited property and agricultural land can involve different records and procedures. A settlement should define shares, possession, expenses and transfer documents clearly. If agreement is not possible, the appropriate partition or other proceeding should include all necessary parties and seek relief that can be implemented against the actual property record.'],
    ['Inheritance Property Disputes Between Legal Heirs', 'Separate Succession Entitlement From Existing Title Problems', 'An inheritance dispute may involve omitted heirs, disputed gifts, alleged relinquishment, possession by one family member or property that was never transferred into the deceased owner’s name. Death and family records should be reviewed together with the property documents. A succession certificate or letter of administration may be relevant to estate administration, but it does not automatically resolve every title or possession dispute. Heirs should obtain advice before signing releases, family settlements or sale authorities that may affect their shares.'],
    ['Property Fraud, Forgery And Challenged Transfers', 'Secure Official Copies And Preserve The Transaction History', 'Where a transfer, signature, authority letter or sale document is challenged, obtain reliable copies from the relevant record and preserve the client’s originals, payment evidence and communications. Counsel should identify the instrument said to be invalid, the persons who benefited from it and any later transfers. Civil remedies and possible criminal allegations require separate legal assessment. Limitation, necessary parties and interim protection should be considered early so the case addresses both the disputed document and its practical consequences.'],
    ['Property Injunctions, Evidence And Court Strategy', 'Coordinate Interim Protection With The Main Property Claim', 'Threatened sale, construction, demolition or interference with possession may justify an application for interim relief where the legal requirements are met. The court will consider the underlying right, supporting evidence and circumstances, so an injunction should not be treated as a stand-alone substitute for the main claim. Clients should disclose earlier suits, orders and settlements. A complete chronology, accurate property description and preserved documentary record help counsel select the correct forum, parties and final relief.'],
  ],
}
